CHANGELOG = '## 0.126.0 - every piece at a bus stop faces the road, and a street phone wears its own booth\n\n**The factory\'s roadmap 210.** The walker\'s look review, 2026-10-19, on the payphone: a street phone should "Always\nface the sidewalk" -- restaurant_row_001\'s faced the storefront behind it -- and "the same same graffiti and drawing\nint he phone booth is too similar/uniform".\n\n**The facing.** The mailbox, the two news racks and the payphone stand at the bus stop, each 0.45 m in from the\nband\'s back edge, so the sidewalk lies between them and the road. Each one\'s face -- the mailbox\'s door, the rack\'s\nwindow, the phone\'s open side -- is Zoo\'s -Y, which at the road\'s angle points -perp: at the road from the L kerb and\nat the buildings from the R kerb, unless it is turned round. `_stop_corner` turned the payphone round on both kerbs\nand the mailbox and racks on neither. An L-kerb phone faced the wall behind it, and an R-kerb mailbox and its racks\ndid the same.\n\n**The booth.** Zoo 1.116.0 draws a payphone in four looks (`module_variants` 4): which tags went up inside the\nenclosure, in which ink, and which stickers made it onto the back panel. A phone\'s look comes from where it stands,\nas a box truck\'s fleet does (0.103.0), so a re-run of a site stands the same booth in the same place.\n\n### Fixed\n- `site_furniture._stop_corner`: every stop-corner piece takes the hydrant\'s pumper rule (0.72.2): no turn on the\n  L kerb, a half turn on the R. A half turn keeps every footprint, so nothing moves along the band and nothing\n  else is placed differently; only these pieces\' yaw changes, on the kerb that was wrong for each.\n\n### Added\n- `site_cover.COVER_VARIANTS["payphone"] = 4`, and `_stop_corner` gives each payphone\n  `site_cover.cover_variant("payphone", at)`. A variant of 0 is written as none, the plain stem every level had\n  before; a non-zero one reaches the phone\'s slot as `variant`, which Zoo spells `_n<variant>` and\n  `cover_module_refs` already resolves, falling back to the plain stem if a Zoo cannot draw it.\n\n### Tests\n- `tests/test_site_furniture.py`:\n  - `test_every_stop_corner_piece_faces_the_road_from_either_kerb` puts a stop on both kerbs of the kerb probe and\n    holds each piece\'s face, by `plate_facing`, toward the road\'s centre line. It fails on 0.125.0 at the L kerb\'s\n    payphone, whose face points away from the road.\n  - `test_a_street_phone_wears_a_booth_picked_by_where_it_stands` walks stops along both kerbs: each phone\'s variant\n    is `cover_variant` of where it stands, the same on a second plan, and the street wears more than two looks (11\n    phones, all four). It fails on 0.125.0, where no phone carries a variant.\n- `tests/test_cover_variants.py`: the variants table holds the payphone\'s four looks beside the box truck\'s.\n- `tests/test_drop_links_reach_the_site.py` pins deli_a03, not deli_a01. Deli Counter 0.237.0 made deli_a01\n  hole-free, and from then this file\'s first test failed on its own pin, not on Lot: run on 0.125.0 it fails the\n  same way. deli_a03 declares the floor hole, the hatch and the stair link the file asks of a shell.\n\n'
OLD_VERSION, NEW_VERSION = 'Lot 0.125.0', 'Lot 0.126.0'


def _sha(b):
    return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()[:16]


def _read(name):
    """The file's LF text and whether it is CRLF on disk; refuses mixed endings and a file that is not the pinned one."""
    raw = (REPO / name).read_bytes()
    crlf, lf = raw.count(b"\r\n"), raw.count(b"\n")
    if crlf not in (0, lf):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: lot/%s has mixed line endings (%d CRLF of %d); nothing written"
                         % (name, crlf, lf))
    text = raw.decode("utf-8").replace("\r\n", "\n")
    if _sha(text.encode("utf-8")) != PINS[name]:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: lot/%s is %s, not the %s this patch was written against; nothing "
                         "written" % (name, _sha(text.encode("utf-8")), PINS[name]))
    return text, crlf > 0


def main(argv):
    # every file worked out and checked before any is written
    out = {}
    for name, edits in EDITS.items():
        text, crlf = _read(name)
        for what, old, new in edits:
            if text.count(old) != 1:
                raise SystemExit("REFUSED: lot/%s: the anchor at %s is there %d times; nothing written"
                                 % (name, what, text.count(old)))
            text = text.replace(old, new)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    for name in NEW_FILES:
        if (REPO / name).exists():
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: lot/%s exists already; nothing written" % name)
    v = REPO / "VERSION"
    if v.read_bytes().decode("utf-8") != OLD_VERSION:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: VERSION reads %r, not %s; nothing written" % (v.read_text(), OLD_VERSION))
    cl = REPO / "CHANGELOG.md"
    craw = cl.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in craw or not craw.startswith(b"## " + OLD_VERSION.split()[-1].encode() + b" "):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: CHANGELOG.md is not LF opening on %s; nothing written" % OLD_VERSION)
    for name, text in out.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    for name, text in NEW_FILES.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    v.write_bytes(NEW_VERSION.encode("utf-8"))
    cl.write_bytes(CHANGELOG.encode("utf-8") + craw)
    print("%s applied: %d files edited, %d written, VERSION, CHANGELOG. Now, in lot/: the "
          "suite" % (NEW_VERSION, len(out), len(NEW_FILES)))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
